        {
          "resource_id": "monster_action",
          "stats": {
            "action_name": {
              "value": "Captivating Song"
            },
            "action_description": {
              "value": "(concentrate, enchantment, mental, primal)\n\nThe harpy cries out an eerie, compelling melody. Each non-harpy creature within 300 feet who can hear the song must attempt a 21 Will save. On a failure, the creature becomes captivated and must spend each of its actions to move closer to the harpy as expediently as possible, while avoiding obvious dangers. If a captivated creature is adjacent to the harpy, it stays still and doesn't act. If attacked by the harpy, the creature is freed from captivation at the end of the harpy's turn.\n\nThe effect lasts for 1 round, but if the harpy uses this ability again on subsequent rounds, it extends the duration by 1 round for all affected creatures. Once a creature succeeds at any save against Captivating Song, that creature is temporarily immune to Captivating Songs for 24 hours."
            },
